INT. COMMUNITY CENTER KITCHEN - NIGHT

Folding tables. Stacked casserole dishes. A wall clock stuck at 8:10.

A MAN IN A GREEN CARDIGAN (60s) stands at the sink, scrubbing a pan. Across the room, GRETCHEN POLLARD (50s, name tag, clipboard) counts paper plates.

GRETCHEN
Okay, everybody, last call for leftovers.

Nobody answers. The room is empty but for the two of them.

GRETCHEN (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Nine hundred and twelve. Who ate a thousand plates?

MAN IN GREEN CARDIGAN
You've got a lot of plates.

GRETCHEN
Do I know you?

MAN IN GREEN CARDIGAN
Walter. Walter Lindqvist. I'm with the Thursday group.

WALTER
Anyway. I'll be done in a minute.

Gretchen tallies. Walter scrubs.

GRETCHEN
You're not on the sign-in sheet, Walter.

WALTER ^
Nobody ever is.

GRETCHEN
(muttering)
Then who's been eating all the pie?

WALTER
I'd say it was me, but I like to be honest.

She checks the clock. Still 8:10. She shakes her head and goes back to counting.
